<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="2">

  <Content>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="1/8" Page="1" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Ext. Noho Rag STudios</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Alec walks away dejected.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="1/8" Page="1" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Ext. NoHo at large</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Shots of Alec’s feet walking pensively. Then elbow pad and hand swinging. Alec fingers the cut in his jacket.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="2/8" Page="1" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="ALEC"></CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Ext. Burbank welcome sign on Chandler</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Alec takes full frame at the Burbank Welcome sign. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Alec</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(with a sigh)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It’s come to this.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Alec enters Burbank.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="2/8" Page="1" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Ext. Burbank at large</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The Spoke </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">Zaruthustra</Text>
      <Text> by </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">Deodato</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Alec wanders the streets of Burbank in slow motion. Heaving “What the fucks” and general disdain at various things in burbank.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A trio of shots with Alec in front of Train Hobby stores. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="2 6/8" Page="1" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="ALEC"></CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="BILL"></CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MAN"></CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Ext. Alley - Day for Night</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Alec stumbles in to frame, more disoriented than tired. He sees a can on fire with a man warming his hands.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Alec approaches.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Man</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I hate these chilly Burbank nights.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Alec begins rubbing his hands over the fire next to the man.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Man (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Damn near 40.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>But what are you gonna do?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Alec</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Been here long?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Yeah. Too long.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Pause.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Alec commiserates.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ALEC</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>How do you do it?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The guy laughs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>When I find out, I’ll tell ya.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Alec laughs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Pause. Alec and the man have a moment to simmer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ALEC</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Is this it?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Jesus man, you didn’t ask me my name yet!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Manners.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Bill Sampson.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>The world’s shit, ain’t it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Alec looks into the fire.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ALEC</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Yeah. Looks that way.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bill leans in.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You only lost your show.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You kept your integrity.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Alec is shocked.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ALEC</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You know who I am?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Bill</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Yes. Even in the far away land of Burbank. I have heard your name, Alec. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Alec throws his thumb over his shoulder.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ALEC</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>They think I’m the devil.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BILL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Good! Wear it with pride.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ALEC</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Hard to feel pride while hunched over a burning garbage can.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BILL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Ouch! There you go again!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Manners!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>This is my home!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ALEC</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Sorry. It’s just.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I’m a news man, who can’t tell the news!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BILL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>But did you really want to?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Sometimes it seemed like you were really trapped behind that desk.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ALEC</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I was proud at the helm.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BILL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You were comfortable!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Like a baby bird in the nest.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ALEC</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>There were protesters!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BILL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And they kicked you out of the nest.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Time to fly.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ALEC</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You’re right.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BILL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You don’t need a news program to make news.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bill hands Alec a GUN.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Alec</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>What the fuck?!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bill pushes Alec off with a message, Alec walks away as Bill shouts louder and louder.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BILL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>The world is shit, Alec!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>There’s no use trying to change that.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Either play by their rules, or get out!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Alec walks out of frame.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
  </Content>

